1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,360
In the mountain south of Seoul, there is a building that the Korean government does not want

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:05,920
you to know about.

3
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:09,200
A psychiatric hospital where 42 people died.

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,920
A place so terrifying that even the Korean military refused to enter it.

5
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,680
The building is sealed.

6
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:17,520
The windows are boarded.

7
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:22,520
And according to hundreds of witnesses, something inside is still alive.

8
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:28,560
This is the story of Gonjiam psychiatric hospital, Korea's most haunted place.

9
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:32,720
And the truth behind it is even more disturbing than the ghost stories.

10
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:38,080
Gonjiam is a small town in Gyeonggi province, about 40 minutes from Seoul.

11
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:43,240
It's surrounded by mountains and dense forests, quiet, isolated.

12
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:46,240
The kind of place where you could hide something.

13
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:49,760
In the 1980s, a psychiatric hospital was built here.

14
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:54,120
It was a private facility, small, with about 40 beds.

15
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:59,440
The patients were mostly people with severe mental illness who had nowhere else to go.

16
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:02,480
For years, the hospital operated normally.

17
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:05,320
But then, something changed.

18
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:10,840
According to local records and later investigations, the hospital director began cutting corners.

19
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:15,880
Staff were underpaid, medications were rationed, patients were neglected.

20
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:20,960
And then, in the late 1990s, the hospital closed its doors.

21
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:23,920
But here's where the story gets complicated.

22
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:27,800
Initially, the hospital closed because of financial difficulties.

23
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:32,960
The director had mismanaged funds and the facility was shut down by local authorities.

24
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:37,400
Unofficially, the stories are very different.

25
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:40,600
1.34 Maakok

26
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,840
The legend begins.

27
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:47,320
After the hospital closed, locals began reporting strange things.

28
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:51,160
Lights flickering in windows, figures moving in the dark.

29
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:55,400
Thousands of screaming coming from inside the abandoned building.

30
00:01:55,400 --> 00:02:01,640
Then, in the early 2000s, Korean ghost hunters and urban explorers began visiting the site.

31
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:08,320
What they found, or claimed to find, turned gonjiam into a national sensation.

32
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:12,980
Videos appeared online showing abandoned wheelchairs, patient records scattered on the

33
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:16,920
floor, and a chilling atmosphere of decay.

34
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:21,200
Some explorers reported feeling an overwhelming sense of dread.

35
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:25,120
Others claimed to see shadowy figures in the hallways.

36
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:29,160
The most famous story involves the hospital director's office.

37
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:33,720
According to legend, the director's chair was found facing the wall as if someone had

38
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:36,480
been sitting in it, watching the door.

39
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:40,640
And on the desk, a patient file was open to a page that read,

40
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:44,360
The patient escaped, do not search.

41
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:49,800
Whether these stories are true or embellished, they spread like wildfire.

42
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:55,160
Gonjiam became Korea's most famous haunted location, the Korean equivalent of Chernobyl

43
00:02:55,160 --> 00:03:00,960
or the Winchester Mystery House.

44
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:05,680
Bartitsompiak, seven.

45
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:12,360
Dukitaw, the facts versus the myth.

46
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:15,520
But here's where we need to separate fact from fiction.

47
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:21,440
In 2018, the Korean government conducted an official investigation into the gonjiam site.

48
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:25,160
What they found was far less dramatic than the ghost stories.

49
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:27,640
First, the number of deaths.

50
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:31,200
The legend says 42 people died at the hospital.

51
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:36,280
The investigation found that the actual number was much lower, and most deaths were from

52
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:40,000
natural causes, not mysterious circumstances.

53
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:44,120
Second, the hospital didn't close because of ghosts.

54
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:48,920
It closed because of financial mismanagement and regulatory violations.

55
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:52,000
The director was investigated for fraud.

56
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,240
Third, the sealed by the government's story is partially true.

57
00:03:56,240 --> 00:04:01,080
After the hospital closed, the local government did restrict access to the site.

58
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:03,600
But not because of paranormal activity.

59
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:09,680
It was because the building was structurally unsafe and trespassers were damaging the property.

60
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:11,560
But here's the twist.

61
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:15,520
The investigation also confirmed something unsettling.

62
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:20,280
There were unusual occurrences at the hospital during its operation.

63
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:24,920
Staff members reported that certain patients exhibited behavior that couldn't be explained

64
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,880
by their diagnoses.

65
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:31,160
And the director himself reportedly became obsessed with occult practices in his final

66
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:33,400
years at the facility.

67
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:37,600
Was the director's interest in the occult a cause of the hospital's problems or a symptom

68
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:40,080
of his deteriorating mental state?

69
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:43,360
The investigation couldn't determine.

70
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:47,040
Chapter 7-Earthwals 9-A-Cock

71
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:51,040
The Gonjiam Movie

72
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:57,040
In 2018, a horror film called Gonjiam Haunted Asylum was released in Korea.

73
00:04:57,040 --> 00:05:02,080
It became one of the most successful Korean horror films ever made, grossing over 20 million

74
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:04,280
dollars at the box office.

75
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:09,400
The film follows a group of web series creators who enter the abandoned hospital to live stream

76
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,240
their experience.

77
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:15,160
What starts as a publicity stunt becomes a nightmare.

78
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:19,800
The film was shot on location at the actual hospital site, and the director has stated

79
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:26,040
that several crew members experienced unexplained phenomena during filming, lights flickered,

80
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:32,040
equipment malfunctioned, and one crew member reportedly refused to enter certain rooms.

81
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:36,920
The film's success reignited interest in the site, and a new wave of urban explorers

82
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:39,320
descended on Gonjiam.

83
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:46,040
The local government, frustrated by trespassers, eventually demolished the hospital in 2018.

84
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:49,040
But the demolition didn't end the stories.

85
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:53,640
Today the site where Gonjiam's psychiatric hospital once stood is empty.

86
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:57,320
The building is gone, but the stories persist.

87
00:05:57,320 --> 00:06:00,960
Some say the spirits were released when the building was demolished.

88
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:06,800
Others say they're still there, in the ground, in the trees, in the air.

89
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:09,480
What we know for certain is this.

90
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:15,360
A psychiatric hospital operated in the mountains south of Seoul for over a decade.

91
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:16,760
People died there.

92
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:23,600
The director may have practiced occult rituals, and when it closed, the stories began.

93
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:28,000
Whether Gonjiam was truly haunted or simply a place where human suffering was concentrated

94
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,200
and amplified, one thing is clear.

95
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:36,240
The line between madness and the supernatural is thinner than we think.

96
